    "# Week 4 - Lab 4: Stokes-to-Navier-Stokes correction\n",
    "\n",
    "<!-- MIE690A article-aligned validation v4 -->\n",
    "\n",
    "This lab uses an actual Stokes solution and Reynolds number to predict the nonlinear correction required by the steady Navier-Stokes solution. It is a data-driven correction experiment, not weight transfer from a Stokes network."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0a8ff764",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Learning goals\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Separate a low-fidelity physical solution from a learned correction.\n",
    "2. Keep Reynolds-number changes consistent with velocity changes.\n",
    "3. Compare constant and spatially diverse lid boundary conditions.\n",
    "4. Evaluate all four train/test family combinations and two out-of-distribution groups.\n",
    "5. Distinguish same-grid surrogate accuracy from mesh-independent CFD validation."
   ]
